.IP "\fBXmNloadModel\fP" 8
As previously discussed, this specifies the loading model to use. Valid
values are:
.RS 8
.IP \(bu 4
\fBXmUNSPECIFIED_LOAD_MODEL\fP \(em The font is user-supplied.
.IP \(bu 4
\fBXmLOAD_DEFERRED\fP \(em Load the font on first use.
.IP \(bu 4
\fBXmLOAD_IMMEDIATE\fP \(em Load the font at XmRendition creation.
.IP \(bu 4
\fBXmLOAD_LAZY\fP \(em Load the font on-demand with \fBXmRenditionLoad\fP.
.RE

.IP "\fBXmNfontType\fP" 8
This indicates the type of font being used and must be one of:
.RS 8
.IP \(bu 4
\fBXmFONT_IS_FONT\fP \(em Plain X font
.IP \(bu 4
\fBXmFONT_IS_FONTSET\fP \(em X fontset
.IP \(bu 4
\fBXmFONT_IS_XFT\fP \(em Xft font
.RE

.IP "\fBXmNtag\fP" 8
.RS 8
Tag (\fBXmStringTag\fP) to use for selecting this rendition for rendering.
This value may be queried, but is fixed once the rendition is created.
.RE

.IP "\fBXmNfont\fP" 8
.RS 8
Depending on font type, \fBXFontStruct *\fP or \fBXFontSet\fP associated
with this rendition, cast to \fBXtPointer\fP.
.RE

.IP "\fBXmNxftFont\fP" 8
.RS 8
\fBXftFont *\fP associated with this rendition, cast to \fBXtPointer\fP.
.RE

.IP "\fBXmNfontName\fP" 8
.RS 8
Specification string for this rendition. For X fonts this will be a
X Logical Font Description (XLFD) string, and for Xft fonts, a
Fontconfig pattern string.
.RE

.IP "\fBXmNfontFoundry\fP" 8
.RS 8
Font foundry string, supplied by the font.
.RE

.IP "\fBXmNfontFamily\fP" 8
.RS 8
Font family string, supplied by the font.
.RE

.IP "\fBXmNfontStyle\fP" 8
.RS 8
Font style string, only supplied by Xft fonts.
.RE

.IP "\fBXmNfontSize\fP" 8
.RS 8
Font size in points, supplied by the font.
.RE

.IP "\fBXmNfontPixelSize\fP" 8
.RS 8
Font size in pixels. For Xft fonts, this is supplied by the font, for X
fonts, this is calculated based on the screen DPI and point size,
.RE

.IP "\fBXmNfontSlant\fP" 8
.RS 8
Slant value supplied by the font. Motif pre-defines the following
constants for convenience:
.IP \(bu 4
\fBXmSLANT_ROMAN\fP \(em Regular, upright slant.
.IP \(bu 4
\fBXmSLANT_ITALIC\fP \(em Right-slanted glyphs which may be narrower than
their roman counterparts, usually inspired by handwriting.
.IP \(bu 4
\fBXmSLANT_OBLIQUE\fP \(em Simply right-slanted versions of roman glyphs.
.RE

.IP "\fBXmNfontWeight\fP" 8
.RS 8
Weight value supplied by the font. Motif pre-defines the following
constants for convenience:
.IP \(bu 4
\fBXmWEIGHT_REGULAR\fP \(em Regular weight.
.IP \(bu 4
\fBXmWEIGHT_MEDIUM\fP \(em Medium weight between regular and bold, ideal
for emphasis.
.IP \(bu 4
\fBXmWEIGHT_DEMIBOLD\fP \(em Darker than medium, lighter than bold.
.IP \(bu 4
\fBXmWEIGHT_BOLD\fP \(em Heavy weight ideal for strong text or headers.
.RE

.IP "\fBXmNwidth\fP" 8
.RS 8
Indicated maximum layout width for a glyph in the font in pixels.
.RE

.IP "\fBXmNinkWidth\fP" 8
.RS 8
Indicated maximum ink width for a glyph in the font in pixels.
.RE

.IP "\fBXmNascent\fP" 8
.RS 8
Indicated ascent value for the font in pixels.
.RE

.IP "\fBXmNdescent\fP" 8
.RS 8
Indicated descent value for the font in pixels.
.RE

.IP "\fBXmNtabList\fP" 8
.RS 8
Specifies the tab list which specifies how compound strings containing
tab components are laid out in columns.
.RE

.IP "\fBXmNrenditionForeground\fP" 8
.IP "\fBXmNrenditionBackground\fP" 8
.RS 8
Specifies the foreground or background color for the rendition, as a
\fBPixel\fP value. A value of \fBXmUNSPECIFIED_PIXEL\fP indiciates that
that particular color is not set for this rendition.

The resource converter for this field (applied when these are loaded via
X resources) expects an X color name, or the special string
"unspecified_pixel".
.RE

.IP "\fBXmNforegroundState\fP" 8
.IP "\fBXmNbackgroundState\fP" 8
.RS 8
If ether of these resources are set to \fBXmFORCE_COLOR\fP, the respective
color specified in the rendition will be preferred over values from other
styles/renditions evaluated when rendering a compound string (or part
thereof). These resources have been present at least as far back as
Motif 2.1.30 and were heretofore undocumented.
.RE

.IP "\fBXmNunderlineType\fP" 8
.IP "\fBXmNstrikethruType\fP" 8
.RS 8
Specifies the line type for striking through or underlining a compound
string. Valid values are:
.IP \(bu 4
\fBXmAS_IS\fP \(em The value is unspecified.
.IP \(bu 4
\fBXmNO_LINE\fP \(em Strikethrough / underline will not be applied.
.IP \(bu 4
\fBXmSINGLE_LINE\fP \(em A single line will be used.
.IP \(bu 4
\fBXmDOUBLE_LINE\fP \(em A double line will be used.
.IP \(bu 4
\fBXmSINGLE_DASHED_LINE\fP \(em A single-dashed line will be used.
.IP \(bu 4
\fBXmDOUBLE_DASHED_LINE\fP \(em A double-dashed line will be used.
.RE

.SH HISTORY
\fBXmRendition\fP was added to Motif sometime around version 2.0 as a
replacement for the prior \fBXmFont\fP abstraction, and was updated
to include support for Xft fonts in Motif 2.3.0. The font metrics and
metadata properties (e.g., \fIXmNascent\fP, \fIXmNfontFamily\fP), along
with \fBXmRenditionStyle\fP were added in version 2.6.0.

